(3108065, 437010, 69008, '<td valign="top">I think that only DSLR people will get the point. Nice composition though, the way the light sweeps you from the lower left to the darker upper right. Rule of thirds you know, LOL. We made me smile.</td>', 'I think that only DSLR people will get the point. Nice composition though, the way the light sweeps you from the lower left to the darker upper right. Rule of thirds you know, LOL. We made me smile.', '2006-12-11 23:11:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108067, 436984, 61818, '<td valign="top">Cute girl in a french maid outfit and this was all you could get out of it?  Stick a duster in her hand, bend her over a dirty table and you meet the challenge and get hottie points as well.  Just think you missed an opportunity here.</td>', 'Cute girl in a french maid outfit and this was all you could get out of it?  Stick a duster in her hand, bend her over a dirty table and you meet the challenge and get hottie points as well.  Just think you missed an opportunity here.', '2006-12-11 23:11:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108085, 436905, 61818, '<td valign="top">I''m just not sure what to make of this.  I actually held off on voting on it after first checking it out last night.  The dirt looks like it was an attempt at making an interesting pattern on the skin, but the processing really makes it look like pudding smeared on her.  Normally I''m all for smeared pudding on naked women, don''t get me wrong, but it''s just not very appealing here.  I think maybe there''s actually too much clean skin showing to present this as some hidden gem ''beneath the dirt''.  Honestly I just can''t get my head around the shot.  Don''t care for the processing, though I can see it being an attempt to make the whole image ''dirty'' in appearance.  I just get the impression you had  vision for this shot and it fell apart in execution.  Then again, maybe you think it''s the cat''s meow and there are 20 other comments agreeing with you.  Good luck!</td>', 'I''m just not sure what to make of this.  I actually held off on voting on it after first checking it out last night.  The dirt looks like it was an attempt at making an interesting pattern on the skin, but the processing really makes it look like pudding smeared on her.  Normally I''m all for smeared pudding on naked women, don''t get me wrong, but it''s just not very appealing here.  I think maybe there''s actually too much clean skin showing to present this as some hidden gem ''beneath the dirt''.  Honestly I just can''t get my head around the shot.  Don''t care for the processing, though I can see it being an attempt to make the whole image ''dirty'' in appearance.  I just get the impression you had  vision for this shot and it fell apart in execution.  Then again, maybe you think it''s the cat''s meow and there are 20 other comments agreeing with you.  Good luck!', '2006-12-11 23:19:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108089, 437086, 61818, '<td valign="top">Cool photo, great capture.  The vignetting along the top really, really needs to go.  Other than that, a strong entry.  Good luck!</td>', 'Cool photo, great capture.  The vignetting along the top really, really needs to go.  Other than that, a strong entry.  Good luck!', '2006-12-11 23:21:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108093, 436985, 69008, '<td valign="top">Nice tomato crop! My current work is assembling and wiring up a machine to wash, wax, and sort tomatoes at the rate of about 900  25lb boxes per hour. Most people don''t know that you mostly get green stained hands from picking tomatoes, but this is a photo contest. Good concept, and excecuted well in the tech dept. I take away one little click for the back light showing behind the lower tomato, right side, and above the top tomato. If you could get that little border around the outside of the hands, like where the leaf on the right goes over the finger, it would really stand the whole subject out from the background.</td>', 'Nice tomato crop! My current work is assembling and wiring up a machine to wash, wax, and sort tomatoes at the rate of about 900  25lb boxes per hour. Most people don''t know that you mostly get green stained hands from picking tomatoes, but this is a photo contest. Good concept, and excecuted well in the tech dept. I take away one little click for the back light showing behind the lower tomato, right side, and above the top tomato. If you could get that little border around the outside of the hands, like where the leaf on the right goes over the finger, it would really stand the whole subject out from the background.', '2006-12-11 23:23:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108096, 436280, 69008, '<td valign="top">Cute idea. Like "Boogers", every body gets them, nobody loves them. No wonder the little feller looks so sad.</td>', 'Cute idea. Like "Boogers", every body gets them, nobody loves them. No wonder the little feller looks so sad.', '2006-12-11 23:25:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108098, 435998, 69008, '<td valign="top">Good pet portrait. Title needs something. It may be a translation problem, and not as you intended it, as I know that this is a world wide website.</td>', 'Good pet portrait. Title needs something. It may be a translation problem, and not as you intended it, as I know that this is a world wide website.', '2006-12-11 23:28:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108101, 436837, 61818, '<td valign="top">Hmm, some problems here.<br/> <br/>You''ve got something with a zero-thought-required relation to the challenge theme.  This is good if you don''t want to take any risks.<br/> <br/>The subject matter is boring.  Very boring.  So the challenge for you is to present it in an interesting manner.  Dead centered and slightly out of focus with nasty shadows and a pea soup background is not the approach to take.<br/> <br/>Perhaps getting in closer, or cropping the image heavily, to present a section of the root ball with the dirt amidst the plant matter - in sharp focus - would work better.  There are some interesting patterns in there.  Shot from straight on or even slightly below would also work better than top down.  Certainly a black (or white maybe) background would also set the subject off nicely and get it to stand out.<br/> <br/>A final consideration is the lighting.  Try setting this next to a window during the day and let the natural light fall on it from the side.  That would accentuate the shadows within the root ball giving the whole thing much more depth and my eye much more to feast upon.<br/> <br/>Hope those are some relatively helpful ideas.  I imagine this photo is probably not setting a scoring record but maybe you are getting comments so you can make some improvements for the next challenge.<br/> <br/>Good luck!</td>', 'Hmm, some problems here. You''ve got something with a zero-thought-required relation to the challenge theme.  This is good if you don''t want to take any risks. The subject matter is boring.  Very boring.  So the challenge for you is to present it in an interesting manner.  Dead centered and slightly out of focus with nasty shadows and a pea soup background is not the approach to take. Perhaps getting in closer, or cropping the image heavily, to present a section of the root ball with the dirt amidst the plant matter - in sharp focus - would work better.  There are some interesting patterns in there.  Shot from straight on or even slightly below would also work better than top down.  Certainly a black (or white maybe) background would also set the subject off nicely and get it to stand out. A final consideration is the lighting.  Try setting this next to a window during the day and let the natural light fall on it from the side.  That would accentuate the shadows within the root ball giving the whole thing much more depth and my eye much more to feast upon. Hope those are some relatively helpful ideas.  I imagine this photo is probably not setting a scoring record but maybe you are getting comments so you can make some improvements for the next challenge. Good luck!', '2006-12-11 23:30:26.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108111, 436993, 69008, '<td valign="top">Right to the point, but not an overly interesting looking dirt patch. For some reason, it''s sharp on the right but unsharp on the left as it goes down the drop off. If you didn''t intend it to be that way, inquire about "depth of field" in the tech help section of the forum. It''s really tricky to get a captivating photo of "real dirt".</td>', 'Right to the point, but not an overly interesting looking dirt patch. For some reason, it''s sharp on the right but unsharp on the left as it goes down the drop off. If you didn''t intend it to be that way, inquire about "depth of field" in the tech help section of the forum. It''s really tricky to get a captivating photo of "real dirt".', '2006-12-11 23:36:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108115, 436141, 69008, '<td valign="top">Like the title. I think that I would have gotten lower, to make the pile look bigger and to get the telephone pole out of the picture. It still is ok though, as the camera was at normal eye level, a natural looking way to see things. Maybe you thought about it and shot it at this angle on purpose. Again, good title for this scene.</td>', 'Like the title. I think that I would have gotten lower, to make the pile look bigger and to get the telephone pole out of the picture. It still is ok though, as the camera was at normal eye level, a natural looking way to see things. Maybe you thought about it and shot it at this angle on purpose. Again, good title for this scene.', '2006-12-11 23:41:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(3108122, 436122, 69008, '<td valign="top">Wish I had this kind of dirt in my yard. I didn''t think about it till too late, but this is almost like my idea, "Quicksand".   The scene would be just a hat on wet ground, and maybe a hand out of the ground. <br/>Good effort, and big depth of field, maybe a little too much, as the background in the corner attracts my eyes away from the foreground. I keep looking up there for something that isn''t there.</td>', 'Wish I had this kind of dirt in my yard. I didn''t think about it till too late, but this is almost like my idea, "Quicksand".   The scene would be just a hat on wet ground, and maybe a hand out of the ground. Good effort, and big depth of field, maybe a little too much, as the background in the corner attracts my eyes away from the foreground. I keep looking up there for something that isn''t there.', '2006-12-11 23:49:18.000000', NULL, 1),
