(3110737, 436846, 69008, '<td valign="top">Good lighting levels for exposure and contrast , but the light looks artificial in color temp. It somehow looks like single band light of strobe instead of rich warm reflected sunlight. Strobe on the backdrop does a lot to kick the plant into the foreground and that looks good. This ain''t a snapshot.</td>', 'Good lighting levels for exposure and contrast , but the light looks artificial in color temp. It somehow looks like single band light of strobe instead of rich warm reflected sunlight. Strobe on the backdrop does a lot to kick the plant into the foreground and that looks good. This ain''t a snapshot.', '2006-12-12 23:18:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(3110751, 435503, 69008, '<td valign="top">If this is a candid snapshot, I''m willing to bet that you got a "dirty" look after the surprise wore off. <br/>Good light with enough reflected into the shadow areas for the right amount of detail there. Got a grin from me.</td>', 'If this is a candid snapshot, I''m willing to bet that you got a "dirty" look after the surprise wore off. Good light with enough reflected into the shadow areas for the right amount of detail there. Got a grin from me.', '2006-12-12 23:25:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(3110768, 434696, 69008, '<td valign="top">Try smaller aperture if your camera allows, and it will bring the foreground into better focus. Another way around it is same shutter speed and higher asa if your camera allows you to set them. <br/>Good observation to find the dirt there. Looks like Everglades muck. It blows everywhere like in your pic when it''s dry.</td>', 'Try smaller aperture if your camera allows, and it will bring the foreground into better focus. Another way around it is same shutter speed and higher asa if your camera allows you to set them. Good observation to find the dirt there. Looks like Everglades muck. It blows everywhere like in your pic when it''s dry.', '2006-12-12 23:34:53.000000', NULL, 1),
